WEBVTT

00:13:00.496 --> 00:13:02.412
The framework was my my colleague,
Phil Tetlock,

00:13:02.746 --> 00:13:06.287
where he observed that whatever
your job or career is,

00:13:06.537 --> 00:13:10.662
that you spend a disproportionate amount
of your time thinking like certain

00:13:10.662 --> 00:13:12.912
professions. He said, look, you know,

00:13:12.912 --> 00:13:16.746
there are moments when we think like
preachers, prosecutors and politicians.

00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:20.829
And I think that that all three
of these mindsets can stand in

00:13:20.829 --> 00:13:23.454
the way of rethinking, because
when you're preaching,

00:13:23.454 --> 00:13:25.204
you're already convinced that
you found the truth.

00:13:25.537 --> 00:13:29.496
And so you don't need to question any of
your assumptions when you're prosecuting.

00:13:29.829 --> 00:13:33.454
You are trying to win your case. That
means the other side is wrong.